# Review record for executor merges (owner 2026-10-16: reviews must actually run before work is accepted).
# Grammar (shared parser: scripts/delegation_check.py parse_line), one record per line:
#   <hex sha, 7-40 chars> <STATUS> <YYYY-MM-DD> <note, at least 1 word>
# STATUS: PASS = the reviewer agent returned PASS. WAIVED = accepted without the reviewer; the note is a
#   reason of at least 4 words, and it is refused for merges touching <module>/src/main/** after the cutoff
#   commit 1fb1ed2. PENDING = a review is running. REVISE = the reviewer asked for changes. REVISED = the
#   REVISE was resolved; the note starts with the fix branch tip sha, which needs its own PASS and must be merged.
# Any other non-#, non-blank line is INVALID and fails the gate. Append-only: the LAST valid line per sha wins.
# Keyed by the executor branch tip (before merge) or the merge commit. Before a merge, the
# require-review-before-merge hook needs PASS (or WAIVED off src/main) for the branch tip; after, the Stop
# hook blocks on a missing or invalid record; `delegation_check.py --ci` also fails on PENDING/REVISE.
# Module source = any <top-dir>/src/** (case-insensitive, renames counted as delete + add). WAIVED only
#   for src/debug, src/test, src/testDebug, src/testRelease, src/androidTest after the cutoff.
# No source change may be made IN a merge commit (conflict resolution, --no-commit extras, amends): resolve
#   conflicts on the executor branch (merge the base into it before review). Octopus merges of source are refused.
# REVISED: the fix must descend from the revised branch tip. A key must resolve unambiguously to its commit.
